I stand in the quiet street.
I no longer know the way.
Then I see a man.
He is walking a dog.
I walk over to the man.
"Excuse me," I say.
"I am looking for Museum Island."
"Can you help me?"
The man stops and smiles.
"Of course," he answers.
"The way is not difficult."
"Go to the crossing here."
"Turn left at the crossing."
"Then just go straight ahead."
"Keep going straight ahead to the water."
He points the way with his hand.
"You will already see the museums there."
"Thank you very much for your help," I say.
"You are very welcome," the man says warmly.
I continue in the direction.
The street leads straight to the water.
